<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-Lehman ups Deutsche forecast.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Lehman ups Deutsche forecast.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Earnings estimates for Deutsche Bank AG were raised at Lehman Brothers, the investment bank said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Following first-half results which beat their expectations, Lehman analysts raised their 1997 earnings per share estimate to 5.50 marks from 4.44 marks and their 1998 estimate to 5.40 marks from 5.20 marks.</p>
<p>However they repeated an &quot;underperform&quot; rating on the stock, arguing that it was overvalued following the recent German banks merger and had &quot;no clear way of improving its strategic situation.&quot;</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
